================================================================================
1. PREREQUISITES
================================================================================

Install Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, either in VirtualBox or as a bare-metal install.

Resources:
  - Ubuntu Desktop download: https://ubuntu.com/download/desktop
  - VirtualBox tutorial:     https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DhVjgI57Ino

NOTE: In VirtualBox, select a base memory of at least 16 GB.

Boot Ubuntu 24.04, then log in and continue with the directions below.


================================================================================
2. DOWNLOAD AEROD SOURCES
================================================================================

NOTE: aerod can be installed and run on bare-metal hardware without the need to
      use CORE/EMANE. The CORE/EMANE installation in Section 4 is required only
      when running aerod inside the network emulation environment; for a
      bare-metal deployment, Section 4 may be skipped.

NOTE: "vX.Y" specifies the release number, e.g., v1.0.

Create ~/src if it does not already exist:

    $ mkdir ~/src; cd ~/src


Method 1 - Download aerod sources via git:

    $ git clone https://github.com/Boeing/aerod.git
    $ cd aerod; git checkout vX.Y


Method 2 - Download aerod sources via tarfile:

Download the tag-specific tarfile from github, then:

    $ tar -xzf ~/Downloads/aerod-vX.Y.tar.gz
    $ rm aerod; ln -s aerod-vX.Y aerod; cd aerod

IMPORTANT: The aerod symbolic link is essential for model runtime.


================================================================================
3. INSTALL ESSENTIAL BUILD DEPENDENCIES
================================================================================

Install essential build dependencies and run/compile time services:

    $ sudo apt install build-essential libtool autoconf git libjansson-dev
    $ sudo apt install rsyslog openssh-server flex bison


================================================================================
4. CORE / EMANE INSTALLATION
================================================================================

Install CORE-9.2.1 and EMANE-1.5.3 on Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. CORE release-9.2.1 and
EMANE v1.5.3 are assumed as the baseline.

NOTE: This section is required only for running aerod within the CORE/EMANE
      network emulation environment. After successfully building and testing
      CORE/EMANE, it is highly recommended to take a VirtualBox snapshot of
      Ubuntu for recovery in case the installation becomes corrupted.


4.1 Clone and Build CORE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    $ export REPO_DIR=~/Documents
    $ cd $REPO_DIR
    $ git clone https://github.com/coreemu/core.git
    $ cd core
    $ git checkout release-9.2.1

    $ sudo apt update && sudo apt install python3.12-venv
    $ ./setup.sh
    $ source ~/.bashrc
    $ inv install


4.2 Install EMANE Build Dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NOTE: Protobuf v3.21.9 (Protobuf library + Protobuf compiler) are part of the
      Ubuntu 24.04 distribution.

    $ sudo apt install cmake
    $ sudo apt-get install git gcc g++ autoconf automake libtool dh-python \
        debhelper python3-setuptools libxml2-dev libprotobuf-dev libpcap-dev \
        libpcre3-dev uuid-dev pkg-config python3-protobuf protobuf-compiler


4.3 Fix setuptools Version
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Re-install setuptools at the proper version.

NOTE: "82" is subject to change and may need to be set to a different value in
      the future. If the EMANE Python bindings are not found, see the workaround
      in Appendix A.

    $ sudo /opt/core/venv/bin/python -m pip uninstall -y setuptools
    $ sudo /opt/core/venv/bin/python -m pip install "setuptools<82"


4.4 Clone and Build EMANE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Clone the EMANE repo:

    $ cd $REPO_DIR
    $ git clone https://github.com/adjacentlink/emane.git
    $ cd emane
    $ git checkout v1.5.3

Install Python bindings:

    $ ./autogen.sh
    $ PYTHON=/opt/core/venv/bin/python ./configure --prefix=/usr
    $ cd src/python/
    $ make -j$(nproc)
    $ sudo /opt/core/venv/bin/python -m pip install .

Build and install EMANE:

    $ cd $REPO_DIR/emane
    $ ./autogen.sh
    $ ./configure --prefix=/usr
    $ make -j$(nproc)
      # if 'make -j$(nproc)' fails w/permissions denied to delete __init__.py:
      $ sudo chown -R "$USER:$USER" src
      $ make -j$(nproc)
    $ sudo make install


================================================================================
5. DPDK INSTALLATION
================================================================================

Download DPDK Latest Long Term Stable (tested with "dpdk-stable-24.11.3"):
  - https://core.dpdk.org/download/

Build reference:
  - https://doc.dpdk.org/guides/prog_guide/build-sdk-meson.html

NOTE: Use "sudo" for meson install and pkg-config.


DPDK pre-installation:

    $ sudo apt install python3-pip python3-pyelftools meson libnuma-dev


Download and extract:

    $ cd ~/src
    $ tar -xf ~/Downloads/dpdk*.xz
    $ cd dpdk-stable-*


Make the following local edits before building:

  1) Edit ./lib/ip_frag/ip_reassembly.h

         Change:  IP_MAX_FRAG_NUM = RTE_LIBRTE_IP_FRAG_MAX_FRAG,
         To:      IP_MAX_FRAG_NUM = 64,

  2) Edit ./lib/ip_frag/rte_ipv6_fragmentation.c

         Change:  unlikely(mtu_size < RTE_IPV6_MIN_MTU))
         To:      unlikely(mtu_size < 1024))


Build and install DPDK:

    $ meson setup build
    $ cd build
    $ ninja
    $ sudo meson install
    $ sudo pkg-config --cflags libdpdk
    $ sudo pkg-config --libs libdpdk


================================================================================
6. KEA INSTALLATION
================================================================================

Kea download:
  - https://www.isc.org/download/#Kea
  - (Download Kea-3.0.2.tar.xz)


Kea pre-installation:

    $ sudo apt install build-essential libboost-all-dev libgtest-dev \
        libmysqlclient-dev liblog4cplus-dev


Extract:

    $ cd ~/src
    $ tar -xf ~/Downloads/kea-3.0.2.tar.xz
    $ cd kea-3.0.2


Kea build/install (follow instructions in "INSTALL"):

    $ meson setup build
    $ meson compile -C build
    $ meson install -C build


================================================================================
7. RADVD INSTALLATION
================================================================================

Download radvd-2.20 from: https://github.com/radvd-project/radvd/releases/

    $ cd ~/src
    $ tar -xf ~/Downloads/radvd-2.20.tar.gz

Follow the build/install instructions in "README":

    $ cd radvd-2.20
    $ sudo apt install -y libbsd-dev
    $ ./configure --prefix=/usr/local --sysconfdir=/etc --mandir=/usr/share/man
    $ make
    $ sudo make install


================================================================================
8. COMPILE AND INSTALL AEROD
================================================================================

Compile the aerod source to generate the aerod binary:

    $ cd ~/src/aerod
    $ make clean
    $ make distclean
    $ ./autogen.sh --enable-aero-dpdk
    $ make
    $ sudo make install


================================================================================
9. ENVIRONMENT SETUP REQUIREMENTS
================================================================================

IMPORTANT: The following steps must be completed before running aerod.


9.1 DPDK Hugepages
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DPDK requires HUGEPAGES support in the host OS. Add the following trailing line
to the end of /etc/sysctl.conf, then reboot the system:

    vm.nr_hugepages = 4000

NOTE: The VM or physical machine running Ubuntu 24.04 MUST have at least 16 GB
      of memory in order to set such a large number of hugepages. If running
      very large CORE emulations runs out of memory, try increasing both the
      above number and the system memory.


9.2 Kea Control Socket
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Kea offers a control UNIX socket that needs to be created in
/usr/local/var/run/kea unless kea is compiled from sources and with an alternate
directory specified. To run from a binary distribution without having to build
from source, disable control socket in the kea configuration file and perform
the following operations on host system before running the aerod config files
in the core-gui:

    $ sudo rm -rf /usr/local/var/run/kea /var/run/kea
    $ sudo mkdir /var/run/kea
    $ sudo ln -s /var/run/kea /usr/local/var/run/kea


9.3 CORE GUI Config Files
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~/src/aerod/conf/coregui/24.04 has sample AERO/OMNI config files. Use the latest
versions found in this directory.

To use the configs in the core-gui, create symbolic link "/usr/local/etc/aerod"
to the top-level directory of the aerod sources:

    $ sudo ln -s ~/src/aerod /usr/local/etc/aerod


9.4 aerod Config Files
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~/src/aerod/conf/files/24.04 has sample aerod config files. These can be
customized for environment specifics.


================================================================================
APPENDIX A: CORE/EMANE PYTHON BINDING WORKAROUND
================================================================================

Workaround for the CORE/EMANE Python binding error. Problem is related to the
version of the setuptools, with the pkg_resources module not being available in
/opt/core/venv because of changes in the setuptools package.


Step 1 - Verify the symptom.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Run the following check to confirm that pkg_resources is indeed missing:

    $ /opt/core/venv/bin/python -c 'import pkg_resources; print(pkg_resources.__file__)'

Expected returns if pkg_resources is missing:

    Traceback (most recent call last):
      File "<string>", line 1, in <module>
    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pkg_resources'


Step 2 - Downgrade the setuptools.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    $ sudo /opt/core/venv/bin/python -m pip uninstall -y setuptools
    $ sudo /opt/core/venv/bin/python -m pip install "setuptools<82"


Step 3 - Confirm the pkg_resources availability (1).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    $ /opt/core/venv/bin/python -c 'import pkg_resources; print(pkg_resources.__file__)'

Expected returns if pkg_resources is available:

    <string>:1: UserWarning: pkg_resources is deprecated as an API. See https://
    setuptools.pypa.io/en/latest/pkg_resources.html. The pkg_resources package
    is slated for removal as early as 2025-11-30. Refrain from using [] package
    or pin to Setuptools<81. /opt/core/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/
    pkg_resources/__init__.py


Step 4 - Confirm the pkg_resources availability (2).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    $ /opt/core/venv/bin/python -c "from emane.events import EventService; print('ok')"

Expected returns:

    /opt/core/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/emane/events/tdmaschedule.py:34:
    UserWarning: pkg_resources is deprecated as an API. See https://setuptools.
    pypa.io/en/latest/pkg_resources.html. The pkg_resources package is slated
    for removal as early as 2025-11-30. Refrain from using this package or pin
    to Setuptools<81. from pkg_resources import resource_filename

The setup should now work.


